# Scramble OpenAPI Documentation Guidelines

Scramble derives the OpenAPI document from the live Laravel application.

## Source and consumers

- The documentation UI is available at `/docs/api`.
- The live JSON document is available at `/docs/api.json`.
- No exported `api.json` is committed or used as the mobile source.
- `mobile-app/openapi-codegen.config.js` builds the schema URL from
  `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL`.

## API changes

- Keep route definitions, controller signatures, validation, resources, and
  return types discoverable by Scramble.
- Use targeted PHPDoc or Scramble attributes only when inference is
  insufficient; follow existing nearby patterns.
- Verify significant contract changes against the live document.
- With the backend running, regenerate the mobile client from `mobile-app/`
  using `pnpm run generate:api`. This also runs TypeScript checking.
- Use `pnpm run quality:api` when the full generated-client quality check is
  required.

`composer export:api` remains available for an optional local export, but an
export is not part of the mobile generation flow and must not be committed.
